// P03.25 (CLAUDE.md lessons): units are shared by every function body that is
// checked in parallel (the unit table, the uniqued unit types, the instances
// of a unit-generic function). The diagnostics must not depend on the number
// of threads or on which thread asks first: same text and order with
// -check-j=1 and -check-j=8 for the rule tests. A generated program with
// errors in many bodies that use the same units and instances is checked with
// 1 to 16 threads in ParallelCheck.UnitChecksDoNotDependOnTheThreadCount
// (diagnostics, type dump with the unit records, export data).
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/same-output.py %gopp %S/units-ops-bad.test %S/units-generics-bad.test %S/units-display.test %S/units-typeset-bad.test
